  <ExpectedResult>^(OK|INFO|n/a)( |$)</ExpectedResult>
</Plugin>
<Plugin>
  <PluginName>30.6 - Docker Engine version</PluginName>
  <PluginDescription>Script item 30, sub-section 30.6. Source: gpu_baseline_check_2.sh:2794-2815 (main_30_33.sh:237-258). docker version --format {{.Server.Version}}, else docker --version. Not found -&gt; INFO. &gt;= 29.9.3 -&gt; OK, below -&gt; FAIL. Verdict = worst result in this sub-section, FAIL &gt; WARN &gt; OK &gt; INFO; the WARN/FAIL lines the script adds to item 30's issues/warns are included. Gate (script lines 28-40): no /proc/driver/nvidia, no nvidia-smi, no /dev/nvidia[0-9]*, no NVIDIA 3D/VGA in lspci -&gt; 'n/a no NVIDIA GPU' (script: PASS, skip item 30). Output: '&lt;OK|INFO|WARN|FAIL|n/a&gt; &lt;observed&gt;'. WARN fails in Bitscan. Changed 2026-11-18: reads the engine version from dockerd --version first (no daemon or socket needed), so it is the engine, not the CLI, version.</PluginDescription>
  <PluginId>1f79edae-dba1-4475-9cfe-4976024ae006</PluginId>
  <Execute timeout="60"><![CDATA[
_ver_num() { printf '%s\n' "${1:-}" | grep -oE '[0-9]+(\.[0-9]+)*' | head -1; }
_ver_ge() {
  _a=$(_ver_num "${1:-}"); _b=$(_ver_num "${2:-}")
  if [ -z "$_a" ] || [ -z "$_b" ]; then return 1; fi
  [ "$_a" = "$_b" ] && return 0
  [ "$(printf '%s\n%s\n' "$_a" "$_b" | sort -V | head -1)" = "$_b" ]
}
V=""; D=""
item() {
