  <PluginDescription>Script item 33, sub-section 33.2. Source: gpu_baseline_check_2.sh:3769-3909 (main_30_33.sh:1212-1352). PF from device/net or GID ndevs; none -&gt; WARN. Per VF in ip link show dev &lt;PF&gt;: spoof checking off -&gt; FAIL, missing -&gt; WARN; trust on -&gt; FAIL, missing -&gt; WARN; vlan 0 or 4095 -&gt; WARN. RoCE v1 GIDs &gt; 0 with a VF lacking PF VLAN or no SR-IOV -&gt; FAIL, else WARN; no v1 -&gt; OK. (The RoCE v1 decision sits in this sub-section of the script.) Verdict = worst result in this sub-section, FAIL &gt; WARN &gt; OK &gt; INFO. Gate (script lines 1136-1158): no RDMA port with link_layer=Ethernet -&gt; 'n/a no RoCE port' (script: PASS, skip item 33). in_container = /.dockerenv or docker|containerd|kubepods|lxc in /proc/1/cgroup. Output: '&lt;OK|INFO|WARN|FAIL|n/a&gt; &lt;observed&gt;'. WARN fails in Bitscan. Changed 2026-11-18: 33.2 RoCE v1 GIDs without SR-IOV are INFO (kernel default); 33.3 shared netns is FAIL only with a container runtime; 33.4 umad/issm on a host is INFO.</PluginDescription>
